[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:93. A Noble Gift]
[00:00.860]Passage 93 | 文章九十三
[00:02.585]A noble gift | 珍贵的礼物
[00:05.225]One of the most famous monuments in the world, | 世界上最著名的纪念碑之一，
[00:09.340]the Statue of Liberty, | 自由女神像，
[00:11.285]was presented to the United States of America in the 19th century | 是在19世纪由
[00:16.360]by the people of France. | 法国人民赠送给美国的。
[00:18.865]The great statue, | 这座伟大的雕像，
[00:21.145]which was designed by the sculptor Auguste Bartholdi, | 由雕塑家奥古斯特·巴托尔迪设计，
[00:25.215]took 10 years to complete. | 历时10年才建成。
[00:28.125]The actual figure was made of copper, | 雕像本身是用铜制成的，
[00:31.655]supported by a metal framework, | 由金属框架支撑，
[00:34.295]which had been especially constructed by Eiffel. | 这个框架是由埃菲尔专门建造的。
[00:38.080]Before it could be transported to the United States, | 在它被运往美国之前，
[00:42.435]a site had to be found for it, | 必须为它找到一个地点，
[00:44.900]and a pedestal had to be built. | 并建造一个底座。
[00:47.470]The site chosen | 选定的地点
[00:49.485]was an island at the entrance of New York Harbor. | 是纽约港入口处的一个岛屿。
[00:52.765]By 1884, | 到1884年，
[00:56.335]a statue which was 151 feet tall | 一座151英尺高的雕像
[01:00.330]had been erected in Paris. | 已经在巴黎建成。
[01:02.980]The following year, | 第二年，
[01:05.040]it was taken to pieces and sent to America. | 它被拆解并运往美国。
[01:08.700]By the end of October 1886, | 到1886年10月底，
[01:12.655]the statue had been put together again, | 雕像再次被组装起来，
[01:15.595]and it was officially presented to the American people by Bartholdi. | 并由巴托尔迪正式赠送给美国人民。
[01:21.120]Ever since then, | 从那时起，
[01:23.200]the great monument has been a symbol of liberty | 这座伟大的纪念碑就一直是自由的象征，
[01:26.445]for the millions of people who have passed through New York Harbor | 对于数百万通过纽约港
[01:30.920]to make their homes in America. | 到美国安家的人来说。